\par
Figure 1: Dump of Block 0015 of P?S/8 Version 8Z for TC08.\fs20\par
\par
Figure 2 shows the last three words of the TFS directory set to the specific values particular to the standard release of P?S/8 Version 8Z for the TC01/TC08 DECtape.  System programs are allocated starting in very low blocks [after certain hard-wired data blocks reserved for various purposes including images of non-system device handlers].  In the standard release of P?S/8 for TC01/TC08 DECtape, all system programs are stored in blocks ending at block 0735.  [Additional blocks 0736 through block 0777 are reserved for future expansion of the system program area.]\par
\par
Word[177] of block 0016 contains the starting block for the first file entered into the TFS directory.  In the stated example, this is block 1000.  As such, the file TCBIN occupies blocks 1000-1017.  The file TCBOOT occupies blocks 1020-1037.  The deleted file [formerly known as FOO, but now the only information is that it was three characters and the third character is O] occupies blocks 1040-1057.  The file BAR occupies blocks 1060-1077.  All blocks from 1100 through 2677 are unallocated as part of a series of available slots.\par
\par
Word[176] of block 0016 contains the high-limit block.  The highest block of the final file allowed in the directory must end just prior to this block.  In this example, the highest file allowed would occupy blocks 2660-2677.\page Word[175] was originally undefined in early releases of P?S/8; however this word was added to make the TFS structure somewhat more robust and allow elements of the keyboard monitor to be coded more easily.  The information is essentially redundant to the high-limit block value in word[176] expressed in a more pragmatic manner.  When the directory is full, attempts to access blocks as high [or higher] than the limit block are not allowed.  This corresponds to the address within the TFS directory where the entry for the disallowed file would have been placed.  The value stored in word[175] is this address expressed in two's complement form.\par
\par
Within the keyboard monitor, the image of the TFS directory is stored in 07000-07377.  Instead of calculating the block of a tentative file and comparing to the high-limit block, this information is the address in memory of the first directory slot not allowed.\fs12\par
\par
